  "statementTechnical": "The Weak Force analogue breaks parity (sin is directional, CP-violating) while preserving time-translation; therefore moral debt is simultaneously irreversible and conserved: ψ_whole → ψ_broken + δ + ν_loss.",
  "statementPlain": "Wrongdoing has a direction — it can't be run backward — and yet its cost doesn't vanish. Both are true at once. You can't undo it, and it doesn't disappear.",
